From c89e3c57c7c1ebc76e2a3dd5db7e155c4aade418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SorinS <ssuciu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] vscode: debug Goose programs through goose-dap

The `goose` debug type ran the program with the JIT and nothing else:
every launch was made noDebug and handed to the Run with JIT task. A
launch is now that only when it says noDebug (the Run with JIT
configuration, Run Without Debugging). Any other `goose` launch debugs
the program: the extension resolves the entry file as Run does
(the configuration's `program`, goose.entryFile, or the active file)
and gives goose-dap -- the DAP proxy in front of lldb-dap from
goose-debugger -- a configuration that builds it with `goose build -g`
into an executable beside it and starts it there. A
DebugAdapterDescriptorFactory runs goose-dap over stdio.

- Settings: goose.debugAdapterPath (empty: goose-dap on PATH) and
  goose.lldbDapPath (passed on as lldbDap). Both are withheld in an
  untrusted workspace, where nothing is debugged.
- Before a session, `goose help build` must list --debug-info and
  goose-dap must be found; otherwise an error says which is missing
  and what to install or set. Run with JIT needs neither.
- The launch passes source, program, build, goose, cwd, args (default
  goose.runArguments), env, and goose.stdlibPath as --stdlib in
  buildArgs; anything else the configuration sets (stopOnEntry,
  showRuntimeFrames, initCommands, ...) goes on to goose-dap as written.
- `breakpoints` for the goose language, so breakpoints can be set in
  .goose files.
- Goose: Debug, a command with a button in the editor title beside Run,
  and a configuration in the Run and Debug picker, launch.json's
  initial configurations and its snippets.
- goose.useRunKeybindings keeps F5 on Run with JIT in a Goose editor;
  with it off, F5 debugs and Ctrl+F5 runs with the JIT.

Test: test/debug.test.js activates the extension against a stub of the
VS Code API: a noDebug launch runs the JIT task as before; any other
resolves to goose-dap's configuration and the factory to goose-dap;
goose-dap or -g missing and an untrusted workspace each give their one
message. The launch configuration it produced, given to goose-dap,
built tests/area.goose with -g, stopped on a breakpoint at line 9 with
main at area.goose:9 on top. The extension-host suite's launch without
noDebug now says noDebug.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
